  "summary": {
   "status": "complete",
   "text": "In a December 2025 NOAA announcement, Jacobs described NOAA’s strategic application of AI as a significant leap in weather model innovation, citing improved accuracy and faster, lower-cost delivery through reduced computational expenses. In March 2024 congressional testimony, Jacobs said AI offered a significant opportunity across numerical weather prediction, including potentially replicating modeling systems, while noting that physics-based models, observations, and data assimilation remain necessary for training data. Jacobs also said in a reported statement that he had been an AI skeptic and is now “bought in,” and in an April 2026 statement he said NOAA would use AI and other technologies to increase efficiency in the ocean economy.",
   "sids": [
    "s1",
    "s5",
    "s6",
